<header><h1>The Naalu Collective: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_naalu">The Naalu Collective</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="telepathic"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Telepathic">Telepathic</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Naalu player retains the Naalu 0 token, even if an effect such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Imperial%20Arbiter"><i>Imperial Arbiter</i></a> law causes them to lose the strategy card it was on. The Naalu player will place the Naalu 0 token on another strategy card in this scenario.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Does the Naalu &lsquo;0&rsquo; token move with the strategy card it is placed on if the card is exchanged with or taken by another player? A: No. The Naalu &lsquo;0&rsquo; token stays with the Naalu or the faction that gained the token through the &lsquo;Gift of Prescience&rsquo; promissory note and is placed on any of that player&rsquo;s strategy cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Placing the Naalu 0 token is mandatory, unless the Naalu player has given it to another player with their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Gift%20of%20Prescience"><i>Gift of Prescience</i></a> promissory note.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Must the Naalu place their 0 initiative token?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; Telepathic has no &lsquo;may&rsquo;, so the Naalu always go first in initiative unless they&rsquo;ve given the token away with Gift of Prescience.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="foresight"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Foresight">Foresight</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Using <sc>Foresight</sc> is not a retreat. As such, it cannot be canceled with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Intercept"><i>Intercept</i></a> action card.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When does Naalu Foresight happen, and where can the ships go?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Intercept doesn&rsquo;t stop it, as it isn&rsquo;t a combat retreat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The command token is not spent. The Naalu player cannot use the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Scepter%20of%20Emelpar"><i>Scepter of Emelpar</i></a>, nor will they gain a trade good if they have the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ground forces may be transported.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 16.1: &ldquo;A unit&rsquo;s capacity value indicates the maximum combined number of fighters and ground forces that it can transport.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling on retreats: &ldquo;the number you can attempt to move out of the system is still limited by your ships capacity.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Skilled Retreat differ from a normal retreat?&rdquo;: &ldquo;ships can pick up ground forces from planets.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships moving out of a gravity rift with <sc>Foresight</sc> must roll for removal.<sup>1,2,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do gravity rifts work &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Each ship that leaves or passes through a rift rolls, and is removed on a 1-3.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;A ship that moves through or out of a gravity rift applies +1 to its move value and then rolls one die.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR quick reference: &ldquo;Each Ship Moving Through or Out of Applies +1 Move and Rolls 1 die.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Ships do not roll for removal if the Naalu player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Codex_IV:~:text=Circlet%20of%20the%20Void"><i>Circlet of the Void</i></a> relic.<sup>11</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>11</sup> Codex IV, Circlet of the Void: &ldquo;Your units do not roll for gravity rifts, and you ignore the movement effects of other anomalies.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If all ships are removed, the strategy token will still be placed in the destination system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the destination system already contains one of the Naalu player&rsquo;s command tokens, the command token from the Naalu player&rsquo;s strategy pool is instead placed in their reinforcements.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;for Foresight the Naalu player still takes a command token from the their Strategy Pool but they place it in their reinforcements instead of on the map. Dane&rsquo;s Answer: That is correct.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>After resolving <sc>Foresight</sc>, play continues to the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> step.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When does Naalu Foresight happen, and where can the ships go?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Right after the other player&rsquo;s ships move in, before Space Cannon Offense.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If the defender leaves with Skilled Retreat or Foresight &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The attacker carries on to bombardment, invasion and production as normal.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (sigmazero13, Dec 8, 2017): &ldquo;that is correct, you would trigger foresight before Space Cannon Offense.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>There is no limit on the number of times <sc>Foresight</sc> may be used each round, as long as the Naalu player has command tokens in their strategy pool.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How often can the Naalu use Foresight, and what triggers it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;As often as they have strategy tokens and an eligible system to move to &mdash; there is no per-round limit.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><sc>Foresight</sc> cannot be used if another player&rsquo;s ships only move through the system that contains the Naalu player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How often can the Naalu use Foresight, and what triggers it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;not a ship merely passing through.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Naalu player may use <sc>Foresight</sc> to move their ships into a system that contains another player&rsquo;s structures but no ships, but cannot commit ground forces to planets in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When does Naalu Foresight happen, and where can the ships go?&rdquo;: &ldquo;They may go to any adjacent system without other players&rsquo; ships, including &hellip; one with only enemy structures, but can&rsquo;t land ground forces there.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="gift-of-prescience"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Gift%20of%20Prescience">Gift of Prescience</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The player with <i>Gift of Prescience</i> retains the Naalu 0 token, even if an effect such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Imperial%20Arbiter"><i>Imperial Arbiter</i></a> law causes them to lose the strategy card it was on. That player will place the Naalu 0 token on another strategy card in this scenario.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Does the Naalu &lsquo;0&rsquo; token move with the strategy card it is placed on if the card is exchanged with or taken by another player? A: No. The Naalu &lsquo;0&rsquo; token stays with the Naalu or the faction that gained the token through the &lsquo;Gift of Prescience&rsquo; promissory note and is placed on any of that player&rsquo;s strategy cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="neuroglaive"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Neuroglaive">Neuroglaive</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player only has other players&rsquo; command tokens in their fleet pool when they trigger Neuroglaive, they must return one of those command tokens to that player&rsquo;s reinforcements.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="hybrid-crystal-fighter"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Fighter:~:text=Hybrid%20Crystal%20Fighter">Hybrid Crystal Fighter</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="matriarch"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Flagship:~:text=Matriarch">Matriarch</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The text of the <i>Matriarch</i> is changed to: &ldquo;During an invasion in this system, you may commit fighters to planets as if they were ground forces. When combat ends, return those units to the space area.&rdquo;<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR errata: &ldquo;The text of the Naalu flagship &lsquo;Matriarch&rsquo; should read as follows: &lsquo;During an invasion in this system, you may commit fighters to planets as if they were ground forces. When combat ends, return those units to the space area.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Naalu fighters fighting with the Matriarch win a ground combat or take control of a planet?&rdquo;: &ldquo;per the errata they return to space when combat ends.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Skootur, Oct 12, 2017): &ldquo;The wording on Matriarch should read &ldquo;When combat ends, return those units to the space area&rdquo;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The committed fighters are returned to the space area when combat ends, and thus will not be on the planet for the <b>Establish Control</b> step. If the Naalu player does not commit at least one ground force to a planet and have it survive the combat, they will be unable to gain control of that planet, and the ground combat will end in a draw.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;The Naalu fighters return to the space area when ground combat ends. If no Naalu ground forces are present, the combat is considered to be a draw, and the Naalu do not gain control of the planet.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Naalu fighters fighting with the Matriarch win a ground combat or take control of a planet?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You need actual ground forces to take control.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Skootur, Oct 12, 2017): &ldquo;they are not supposed to establish control of a planet without ground force assistance.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any structures on the planet will not be destroyed if the Naalu player committed no ground forces.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What happens to space docks and PDS when an enemy takes the planet?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Fighters fighting via the Naalu flagship don&rsquo;t destroy them, since they aren&rsquo;t on the planet afterwards.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (sigmazero13, Sep 17, 2018): &ldquo;The Space dock would not be destroyed, in this instance, for the reason you have stated.&rdquo; Fighters-only invaders are never contained by the planet.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies"><i>Dacxive Animators</i></a> technology will not allow the Naalu player to gain control of a planet without committing a ground force.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Using &lsquo;The Matriarch&rsquo; flagship in combination with the &lsquo;Dacxive Animators&rsquo; technology, can the Naalu gain control of a planet using only fighters? A: No. Because the combat ends in a draw, the &lsquo;Dacxive Animators&rsquo; ability is not triggered.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Naalu fighters fighting with the Matriarch win a ground combat or take control of a planet?&rdquo;: &ldquo;If only fighters remain, the combat is a draw, Dacxive Animators doesn&rsquo;t trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Skootur, Oct 12, 2017): &ldquo;Daxcive Animators does not trigger (the combat must be won).&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The committed fighters may be assigned hits during the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Fighters committed to a planet use their own combat value, including that of any fighter unit upgrade.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What combat value do Naalu fighters use in ground combat &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Their own fighter combat value, upgrades included.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="zeu" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Leaders:~:text=Z%27eu">Z&rsquo;eu</a> (replaced by &Omega;) <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
