        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>12</sup> Codex III p. 13, &ldquo;The Omega Initiative&rdquo;: &ldquo;These cards can be found in the high-quality PDF found alongside this document. They are standard American mini cards, and replace their corresponding counterparts from the Prophecy of Kings expansion.&rdquo; The Omega Initiative contents (p. 3) list &ldquo;Z&rsquo;eu&rdquo;.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="zeu-omega" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Leaders:~:text=Z%27eu">Z&rsquo;eu &Omega;</a> (replaced by &Omega;&Omega;) <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega;&Omega; version.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook, integrating the codex cards: &ldquo;If you do have a previous version of the Twilight Codex, simply replace all of its components with the updated versions included in Thunder&rsquo;s Edge.&rdquo; The Thunder&rsquo;s Edge codex card is Z&rsquo;eu ΩΩ.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>All other rules applying to tactical actions apply, other than placing a command token.<sup>12</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>12</sup> Codex III, Z&rsquo;eu Ω: &ldquo;that player may perform a tactical action in a non-home system without placing a command token.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The system cannot already contain a command token for the player performing the tactical action.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 5.2: &ldquo;A player cannot activate a system that already contains one of their command tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>A player may play a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Ceasefire"><i>Ceasefire</i></a> promissory note or discard the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Peace"><i>Minister of Peace</i></a> law for their effects.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If a player uses Z&rsquo;eu &Omega; to activate a system containing another player&rsquo;s units, that will count for the purposes of returning promissory notes, and other similar effects.<sup>12</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>12</sup> Codex III, Z&rsquo;eu (Naalu agent): &ldquo;that player may perform a tactical action in a non-home system without placing a command token; that system still counts as being activated.&rdquo; system counts as activated.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The chosen player is considered to be the active player.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the chosen player is not the Naalu player, it is not considered their turn for game effects.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the tactical action granted by the Codex Naalu agent use a token &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The tactical action happens during the Naalu player&rsquo;s turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player is chosen, and owns their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Yssaril_Tribes#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Transparasteel%20Plating"><i>Transparasteel Plating</i></a> faction technology, other players may still play action cards during the action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the chosen player is not the Naalu player, they may use any &ldquo;before/after you perform an action&rdquo; abilities.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the chosen player is not the Naalu player, they cannot use the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Fleet_Logistics"><i>Fleet Logistics</i></a> technology to perform an additional action.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The chosen player may use the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Master%20Plan"><i>Master Plan</i></a> action card or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20War"><i>Minister of War</i></a> agenda to perform an additional action.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the chosen player is able to perform a component action, they may then use the ability of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Suffi%20An">Suffi An</a>, the <a href="/F_keleres">Keleres</a> commander, to perform additional actions.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the chosen player is not the Naalu player, and they had previously passed, they are still considered passed during their action. They do not pass at the end of the action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The chosen player cannot score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Prove%20Endurance"><i>Prove Endurance</i></a> secret objective at the end of their action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player owns their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Yssaril_Tribes#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Transparasteel%20Plating"><i>Transparasteel Plating</i></a> faction technology, and uses the ability of Ssruu, their agent, to duplicate the ability of Z&rsquo;eu &Omega;, choosing a player that has passed, the chosen player cannot play action cards during their action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Any deal between the Naalu player and another player regarding which system will be activated, if made before Z&rsquo;eu &Omega; is exhausted, is non&ndash;binding.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 28.4: &ldquo;If the terms of a deal cannot be resolved immediately, it is a non-binding deal.&rdquo; system activation happens later, so it cannot be resolved immediately.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Peace"><i>Minister of Peace</i></a> agenda and the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player&rsquo;s Starlancer mech still end the chosen player&rsquo;s tactical action, even though it is not considered their turn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="zeu-omega-omega"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Leaders:~:text=Z%27eu">Z&rsquo;eu &Omega;&Omega;</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Z&rsquo;eu &Omega;&Omega; may be used whenever a command token is placed in a system. For example, it may be used when a player activates a system, when a player resolves the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card, or when a player resolves the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Signal%20Jamming"><i>Signal Jamming</i></a> action card.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
