<h2 id="maban" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Leaders:~:text=M%27aban">M&rsquo;aban</a> (replaced by &Omega;) <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>12</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>12</sup> Codex III p. 13, &ldquo;The Omega Initiative&rdquo;: &ldquo;These cards can be found in the high-quality PDF found alongside this document. They are standard American mini cards, and replace their corresponding counterparts from the Prophecy of Kings expansion.&rdquo; The Omega Initiative contents (p. 3) list &ldquo;M&rsquo;aban&rdquo;.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When producing units, the Naalu player must produce all the units they intend to produce before they may unlock M&rsquo;aban. M&rsquo;aban cannot be applied to the instance of producing the units that unlocks it.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I unlock the Naalu commander partway through a production and use it for the rest?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; production is one step, so the unlock condition is only met after it finishes; use the commander from your next production.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>For example, before production, the Naalu player has ten fighters on the game board. They pay two resources during production. They cannot produce two fighters, unlock M&rsquo;aban, then produce three more fighters. Instead, they would produce all four fighters, and then unlock M&rsquo;aban.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I unlock the Naalu commander partway through a production and use it for the rest?&rdquo;: &ldquo;production is one step, so the unlock condition is only met after it finishes&rdquo; the example follows directly from this rule.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Regulated%20Conscription"><i>Regulated Conscription</i></a> law is in play, the Naalu player may produce two fighters for one resource. This will count as one toward their <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> limit.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a game effect instructs the Naalu player to produce ships without using the <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability, they may only produce additional fighters if that game effect allows them to produce fighters.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Naalu player may choose to produce one fighter for one resource. If they do, they may produce one additional fighter.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Naalu Collective commander, M&rsquo;aban, or the Yin Brotherhood commander, Brother Omar, allow the player to choose to produce only 1 infantry/fighter and then another with their commander? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do the Yin and Naalu commanders&rsquo; extra infantry and fighters work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;When producing those units you may produce one extra for its cost, outside your Production limit.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="maban-omega"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naalu_Collective#Leaders:~:text=M%27aban">M&rsquo;aban &Omega;</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
